# Nesting is recursion in the parser, and nothing counted it: Python's stack
# ran out first, at between 165 and 495 levels depending on the construct, and
# the program left as a RecursionError traceback. The next line opens exactly
# 200 lists, which is the limit. The '[' on the line after it is the 201st and
# is where the guard fires -- so the file is deliberately unbalanced, because
# the parse never reaches a closer.
